<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine mills buy 25,000T U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Philippine mills buy 25,000T U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Philippine mills bought a total of 25,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat through Japanese trading firm Marubeni Corp, Manila grains traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The transaction was made late last week,&quot; an executive in one of the mills told Reuters.</p>
<p>Traders said one of the buyers bought 18,000 tonnes western white wheat for June shipment.</p>
<p>Other details of the deal were not immediately available.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936</p>
